    "content" : "4. SIMULATION AND RESULTS"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 26,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 69.667, 641.223, 290.0, 801.557 ],
    "font" : "Times New Roman",
    "font size" : 9.96,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]",
    "content" : "Various contingencies are simulated on the TNEB as given below. The contingencies include large transient event like three phase fault and contingencies like single line to ground fault are considered. The system has been modeled with existing AVR, governor and PSS and studies are carried out. Rotor angle, voltage and frequency oscillations are considered as key criteria (parameters) to compare the results. Then this system with various AVR, Governor and PSS model and parameters are considered to evaluate their behavior. Best suitable model and parameters of AVR, Governor and PSS is identified based on the above said criteria."
  }, {
    "type" : "heading",
    "pdfua_tag" : "H1",
    "id" : 27,
    "level" : "Subtitle",
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 71.0, 627.223, 164.333, 641.557 ],
    "heading level" : 1,
    "font" : null,
    "font size" : 12.0,
    "content" : "4.1 Three phase fault"
